# Replay corpus entry: envelope-full (replay-command format v1).
#
# The first committed replay in the production replay-command format
# (src/CommandoWar.Sim/ReplaySerialisation.fs, TASK-025 / backlog B-045). It
# carries a full accepted-command envelope the legacy .cwlog cannot express:
# a three-recipient MoveTo (agents 3, 4, 5), Urgency = immediate,
# RiskTolerance = aggressive, issued on tick 1 and delivered on tick 2.
#
# Initial state: the shared spike fixture (Setup.sixAgentWorld, 32 x 32,
# seed 20260902) — resolved by name from Corpus.all, not serialised.
#
# canonical 15 and every hash below were re-pinned by TASK-067 (backlog
# B-067; Canonical.FormatVersion 14 -> 15, ReceivedOrder.AsGroup added).
# This entry's one command addresses three recipients (3, 4, 5) with a
# genuine Command.moveToMany, but none of them authors a FormationOffset
# (Setup.sixAgentWorld has no formation), so AsGroup being true or false
# makes no difference to the resolved target either way: the byte-layout
# change is the only difference, the 24 ticks and 78 domain events are
# unchanged. Prior re-pin: TASK-065 (Canonical.FormatVersion 13 -> 14,
# AgentState.StalledTicks added).
